2. LICENSOR IP VS. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------
The Software is composed of two distinct categories of material, and this
Agreement's ownership and licensing terms apply differently to each:

  (a) Licensor IP: the REST API surface, catalog/dataset/table/job
      orchestration logic, the BigQuery Storage API implementation, the
      materialized-table caching layer, client-conformance work, and all
      other original source code, documentation, and design authored by or
      for the Licensor. This is the material Section 1's ownership claim
      covers, and the material this Agreement's restrictions in Section 5
      protect.
  (b) Third-Party Components: every open-source dependency the Software is
      built on or distributed with (each under its own license — MIT,
      Apache License 2.0, BSD, or similar permissive terms; none copyleft),
      including without limitation the real Google `google/googlesql`
      (GoogleSQL/ZetaSQL) query engine that the Software runs by way of a
      dependency chain through `goccy/go-googlesql` and
      `goccy/googlesqlite`. The Licensor does not own, and does not claim
      to own, any Third-Party Component — the Licensor's rights over a
      Third-Party Component extend only as far as that component's own
      license permits, same as any other user of it. The complete,
      itemized inventory of Third-Party Components and their licenses is
      maintained in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`, and the specific attribution
      required for the Google GoogleSQL engine is set out in `NOTICE` —
      both are incorporated into this Agreement by reference and must be
      preserved, unmodified, in any copy or distribution of the Software.

Nothing in this Agreement restricts You from independently obtaining, using,
or distributing any Third-Party Component under its own separate license,
outside of the Software — this Agreement only governs the Software as
